WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.662
Most beginner NumPy errors come from a small number of concepts.

00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:10.272
The first is shape: two arrays may not have compatible dimensions.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:17.717
The second is data type: values that look numeric may be stored differently than expected.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:23.533
The third is axis: a summary may be calculated in the wrong direction.

00:00:24.169 --> 00:00:33.321
Broadcasting can also produce confusion when shapes are technically compatible but the operation does not match the

00:00:33.321 --> 00:00:38.641
intended meaning. Finally, views can modify original data unexpectedly.

00:00:38.641 --> 00:00:47.806
A strong debugging habit is to print or inspect shape, data type, and a few sample values before changing the code.

00:00:47.806 --> 00:00:51.626
Understanding the structure is usually faster than guessing.
